<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7878" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνδραγαθ-ίζομαι</span></b> , aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνδραγαθίσασθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					App.
					<u>BC</u>
					5.101
				</span></i>
			:—<i>act uprightly,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴ τις ἀπραγμοσύνη -ίζεται</span> if
			any one thinks to sit at home and <i>play the honest man,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.63
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ τοῦ ἀκινδύνου ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					3.40
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>VV</u>
				1250b4
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
